# UI/UX Pro Max Rules (nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill)

## 1. Full-Width Canvas for Admin Tables
- Do not constrain data tables with artificial narrow widths (`max-w-7xl mx-auto`).
- Use uniform dashboard outer padding (`p-6` or `p-8`) across sibling pages.
- Ensure horizontal tables are wrapped in `<div className="overflow-x-auto">`.

## 2. Table Architecture
- Standardize thead with executive primary-dark style (`bg-primary-dark` / `#05445e` with white uppercase text).
- Use generous cell padding (`px-6 py-4`).
- Differentiate row states:
  - Critical/Urgent: `bg-red-50/70 hover:bg-red-100/70`
  - Warning/Pending: `bg-amber-50/40 hover:bg-amber-100/40`
  - Normal: `bg-white hover:bg-slate-50`

## 3. Filter Grid Standard
- 5-Column filter grid: `grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-4 mb-6`.
- SearchableSelect / library-styled dropdowns.
- Clear search input with left icon.

## 4. Typography & Numbers
- Strict `font-mono tabular-nums` for all dates, times, NIP/NIK, scores, and countdowns.
- High-contrast rounded-full status badges.

